+  reported, never assumed complete. The post-run pin check is always attempted and recorded; drift is flagged and does not change
+  the marker. **Output cap enforcement:** `RLIMIT_FSIZE` (4 MiB per file) is set by `prlimit` and applies to the runner's writes to
+  stdout, stderr and artifacts (prevention, per file); the runner keeps its own running total of bytes it writes and stops at
+  8 MiB (prevention, total); the launcher's `du` check against 10 MiB, made before the marker is chosen, is detection. Exceeding any of these yields FAILED
+  and an `OUTPUT_CAP` file. Oracles run in the same process under the same wall, memory and output limits.
